{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:7498521 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:7498521 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"7498521","source":"MED","pmid":"7498521","doi":"10.1016/0014-5793(95)01184-g","title":"Amino acid sequence and expression of the hepatic glycogen-binding (GL)-subunit of protein phosphatase-1.","authorString":"Doherty MJ, Moorhead G, Morrice N, Cohen P, Cohen PT.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Doherty MJ","lastName":"Doherty","firstName":"M J","initials":"MJ","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biochemistry, University of Dundee, Scotland, UK."}]}},{"fullName":"Moorhead G","lastName":"Moorhead","firstName":"G","initials":"G"},{"fullName":"Morrice N","lastName":"Morrice","firstName":"N","initials":"N"},{"fullName":"Cohen P","lastName":"Cohen","firstName":"P","initials":"P"},{"fullName":"Cohen PT","lastName":"Cohen","firstName":"P T","initials":"PT"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7632-9492"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"375","journalIssueId":904508,"dateOfPublication":"1995 Nov","monthOfPublication":11,"yearOfPublication":1995,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"FEBS Lett","title":"FEBS letters","essn":"1873-3468","issn":"0014-5793","nlmid":"0155157","isoabbreviation":"FEBS Lett"},"printPublicationDate":"1995-11-01"},"pubYear":"1995","pageInfo":"294-298","abstractText":"A full-length cDNA encoding the putative hepatic glycogen-binding (GL) subunit of protein phosphatase-1 (PP1) was isolated from a rat liver library. The deduced amino acid sequence (284 residues, 32.6 kDa) was 23% identical (39% similar) to the N-terminal region of the glycogen-binding (GM) subunit of PP1 from striated muscle. The similarities between GM and GL were most striking between residues 63-86, 144-166 and 186-227 of human GM (approximately 40% identity), nearly all the identities with the putative yeast homologue GAC1 being located between 144-166 and 186-227. The cDNA was expressed in E. coli, and the expressed protein transformed the properties of PP1 to those characteristic of the hepatic glycogen-associated enzyme. These experiments establish that the cloned protein is GL.","affiliation":"Department of Biochemistry, University of Dundee, Scotland, UK.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Muscle, Skeletal","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Liver","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Rabbits"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Rats"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Macromolecular Substances"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Liver Glycogen","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Glutathione Transferase","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"BI","qualifierName":"biosynthesis"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Phosphorylase a","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Carrier Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"BI","qualifierName":"biosynthesis"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic